{"author":{"id":"40e3ba2788b3b9fc163c354afc44e5f9d225bcf0a27e679aaa878dd6135c6dcb"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1781183673,"nonce":"RpjcwhKc2D6xeyjNe80acDa7QQg=","title":"ftell offsets truncated to 32-bit unsigned: archives \u003e4GB silently corrupt at create","message":"Audit finding (NetBSD portability sweep, 2026-06-11), verified real. cli/src/main.c lines ~1292/1309/1434 cast ftell(out) (64-bit long) to unsigned for master/file/cdir offsets; positions past 4GiB wrap silently and the directory points at wrong offsets. The UC2 container itself uses 32-bit offsets, so the honest fix is a loud error when the output position would exceed 0xFFFFFFFF (and an ftell error check at uc2_ingest.c:195 which currently stores -1 unchecked). Multi-volume spanning (issue 2b65f0a) is the real path for \u003e4GB payloads.","files":null}]}